.tl 'MACRO(I)'12/17/75'MACRO(I)'


NAME
	macro - macro assembler for UNIX

SYNOPSIS
	macro [options] file1 file2 ... filen

DESCRIPTION
.in 8
Macro assembles the concatenation of the specified files terminating when an ".end"
statement is encountered. The resulting file is named "filen.obj." If a file arg
does not contain a ".", file "file.m11" will be sought before "file" itself.

Options, if desired, may appear anywhere in the command, and are chosen from the following:

.mk
.in 12
1) -ls
.br
.in 22
.rt
Produce an assembly listing named "filen.lst"
.br
.in 12
.mk
2) -cr
.br
.in 22
.rt
Produce a cross-reference listing named "filen.lst". If -ls
is also specified, the cross-reference listing is appended to the
assembly listing.
.br
.in 12
.mk
3) -no
.br
.in 22
.rt
No object file is produced. This is useful for syntax checking, or listing only.
.br
.in 12
.mk
4) -xs:n
.br
.in 22
.rt
Allocates an extra nK words of space for symbol table and macro storage.
.br
.in 12
.mk
5) -ns
.br
.in 22
.rt
No symbol output information is produced in the object modules.
.br


.in 0
FILES
	/etc/sysmac.sml - system macro library (for .mcall)
	filen.xrf - intermediate cross reference temporary
	/bin/macxrf - cross-reference processor

SEE ALSO
	DEC Macro-11 Manual
